{"title":"2017 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Prime_Factorization)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Prime Factorization)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Splitting)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Splitting)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Units_Digit)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Units Digit)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/9/be932a531ce98b59d2031a0e343197f054aa26ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44 \\times 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> is equal to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3aad2dd5eac2e8d951598329fcd6955c2b7000b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 88 \\times 2 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 88 \\times 11 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 88 \\times 20 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 88 \\times 44 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 88 \\times 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"589\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/4/614be2a41353cfefcf40e5866dd763bd079253aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44 \\times 22 = 968$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" />, so we can look at the different answer choices until we get one that matches.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/4/fb4eb7456413a799b6cf1fc56f86f3f45485b27c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$88 \\times 2 = 176$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />, so this can't be the answer.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87f2dc4902bcd5bf591d1f2dfebe1f2b042ccdc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$88 \\times 11 = 968$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" />, which happens to be equal, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/b/68b30db159515325208dc2e70f411fe15851c2fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } 88 \\times 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"107\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Prime_Factorization.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Prime_Factorization)\">Solution 2 (Prime Factorization)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Prime Factorization)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/a/92a70d3843d5e31538013f316b32d1de9b476b10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44 \\times 22 = 2^{2} \\times 11 \\times 2 \\times 11 = 2^{3} \\times 11^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"302\" height=\"18\" />. We can then look at the answer choices until we get one that matches.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/f/98f0bf485f9c7207f30f23b9ed279c932886484a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$88 \\times 2 = 2^{3} \\times 11 \\times 2 = 2^{4} \\times 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"245\" height=\"18\" />. This doesn't match, so this can't be right.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/b/27bcf1458323a4f569b9afc5f420c999a5fa156a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$88 \\times 11 = 2^{3} \\times 11 \\times 11 = 2^{3} \\times 11^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"271\" height=\"18\" />. This matches the original prime factorization, so the answer must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/2/7a297ce028afcd148bbb01bcedcde1ea1c9ae6b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 88 \\times 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"107\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Splitting.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Splitting)\">Solution 3 (Splitting)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Splitting)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b1a22dbff35f958bb5bd79d96ceff780b94f853.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22 = 2 \\times 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/5/3656319bea781c540e040388450be438ad0f809e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44 \\times 22 = 44 \\times 2 \\times 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"175\" height=\"15\" />, which is the same as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/b/68b30db159515325208dc2e70f411fe15851c2fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } 88 \\times 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"107\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Units_Digit.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Units_Digit)\">Solution 4 (Units Digit)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Units Digit)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/9/be932a531ce98b59d2031a0e343197f054aa26ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44 \\times 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> has the same units digit as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d037bd49957923de4c5fb6cac7257f72b4dc64a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 2 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />, so the answer choice must also have the same units digit. Of the answer choices, the only one that this is true for is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/b/68b30db159515325208dc2e70f411fe15851c2fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } 88 \\times 11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"107\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher \n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" co